@intent The Last Sword's story, played stage by stage as a player would: the troubled blacksmith in a village and his scroll, the dragon cult's raid on that village and its victory, the secret letter that points to the Nether, the traveler's hold and its message, the End's ruins and sealed spire, freeing the Lost Wraith, the note that leads to the Wound of Time, and the queen's trial -- each stage gated on the advancement the mod grants for it
@continue-on-fail
@world flat structures
# the audio device complains when many sounds stop at once on arriving somewhere: not the mod's
@allow error OpenAlUtil
# the item frames in the traveler's hold and the sealed spire carry the authors' world coordinates (TileX/Y/Z), so
# generation logs one ERROR each (PLAN.md): known, not what this script tests
@allow error Block-attached entity at invalid position
# their entities also carry Forge 1.20.1 attribute ids (forge:step_height_addition, forge:entity_gravity) that 1.21 no
# longer has: one ERROR per attribute as they load (PLAN.md; entity_gravity seen once, 1.21.5 r3, in the hold)
@allow error forge:(step_height_addition|entity_gravity)
# The world is vanilla's superflat: the overworld has villages (enough for the blacksmith and the raid), and the Nether
# and the End generate normally, the mod's structures included. Travel is @goto (vanilla /locate); every stage's
# mechanic is the player's own doing. One stage is not reached here: the ruined village is placed only by the normal
# overworld's worldgen (and /place registers no structure, so its "discover" check would never fire).
# Stages run in order. Loops (@repeat each ... until) strike each mob until it falls, always within a bound; each run
# puts the sword back in hand (after it kills one of the mod's mobs the sword leaves the hand -- the mod's design).

@step S1 welcome, and the village hint
gamemode survival
difficulty hard
difficulty normal
time set day
weather clear
gamerule doDaylightCycle false
gamerule doMobSpawning false
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 99999 4 true
effect give @s minecraft:regeneration 99999 1 true
effect give @s minecraft:saturation 99999 0 true
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:the_last_sword_welcome=true}]
# 60 ticks after the welcome, the mod points to the nearest village
@expect chat message.the_last_sword.nearest_village_location within 10s
@shot welcome

@step S2 the troubled blacksmith appears in the village
# entering any village piece for the first time spawns him (a level-5 weaponsmith) and grants the stage
@goto structure #minecraft:village
@expect chat message.the_last_sword.troubled_blacksmith_intro within 10s
# @goto puts the player inside the village's start piece, which is its well: step out onto open ground nearby
# (still in the village) so the trade and the raid are not fought from inside the well's walls
spreadplayers ~ ~ 0 10 false @s
@wait 2s
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:troubled_blacksmith=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:troubled_blacksmith=true}]
@assert execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}}]
@shot blacksmith

@step S3-S4 buy The Last End Scroll from him
# his first offer: 1 emerald for the scroll. Slots of the trade screen: 0-1 payment, 2 result, 30 the first hotbar slot
give @s minecraft:emerald 1
# meet him on a platform above the village: on the ground a wall or a counter can stand between the two (the crosshair
# then lands on a block). Freeze him first, then step up to him: the player arrives last, so neither has moved
execute as @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}}] run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}},limit=1,sort=nearest] run fill ~-3 ~12 ~-3 ~3 ~12 ~3 minecraft:smooth_stone
execute as @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}},limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s run tp @s ~ ~13 ~
@wait 15t
execute as @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}},limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp @p ^ ^ ^1.8 facing entity @s
@wait 5t
@aim entity @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}},limit=1,sort=nearest]
@wait 2t
@aim entity @e[type=minecraft:villager,nbt={VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:weaponsmith",level:5}},limit=1,sort=nearest]
@key key.use
@expect screen Merchant within 3s
@shot trade-screen
@click slot 30
@click slot 0
@wait 5t
@click slot 2
@click slot 31
@wait 5t
@key key.keyboard.escape
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:the_last_end_scroll_obtain=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:the_last_end_scroll
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:the_last_end_scroll_obtain=true}]
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:mage_village_destination=true}]

@step S5 the ruined village (its own script)
# placed only by the normal overworld's worldgen: a superflat world never has one. 12-ruined-village.playtest plays
# it in a normal world (the discovery, and the crystal from the wizard tower's frame)
@wait 1t

@step S6 a dragon crystal
# the raid (next stage) starts only while the player is inside a village piece: back to the village's centre (its
# well) before the crystal, rather than wherever stepping out of the well landed (measured: at the village's edge,
# outside every piece, the raid never started)
@goto structure #minecraft:village
# the stage takes a slot that changes to exactly 1 crystal; the ruined village's item frame is the story's source
give @s the_last_sword:dragon_crystal 1
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:dragon_crystal_obtain=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:dragon_crystal_obtain=true}]

@step S7 the dragon cult attacks the village
# carrying a crystal inside the village starts the raid within 2 s (the quest handler's 40-tick check)
@expect bossbar raid.the_last_sword.dragon_cult_raid within 10s
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:dragon_cult_raid=true}]
@shot raid

@step S8 the raid is won
# three waves: 2 cultists; 1 paladin and 3 cultists; 1 priest, 2 paladins and 3 cultists, 15 s apart. Each raider is held
# still once it arrives (its fight is the raid's) and struck with the mod's sword until it falls; the paladins and the
# priest take many capped hits by design, so their bounds are high
# the fight happens on open ground built for it, 12 blocks above the village: a clear line of sight to every raider
# (measured: in the village, raiders teleported in front of the player landed in walls, a bell, the ground). The
# raid's centre stays in the village, which is all its rules check; raiders are brought up to the platform to be struck
fill ~-5 ~12 ~-5 ~5 ~12 ~5 minecraft:smooth_stone
tp @s ~ ~13 ~
@wait 1s
# each raider is struck from 2.8 blocks: inside melee reach (3), outside the pickup radius, so its drops stay on the
# ground (S9 collects the letter) instead of flooding the hotbar into the sword's slot. The sword lives in the last hotbar slot: after a kill it leaves the hand (the mod's design), drops are picked up into
# the first empty slots, and re-arming writes only its own slot (re-arming the main hand would overwrite a picked-up
# drop -- measured: the priest's letter, lost that way)
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
# wave 1: let its raiders arrive, then strike each one until it falls
@wait 4s
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cultist,distance=..64] max 6 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_paladin,distance=..64] max 40 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_priest,distance=..64] max 60 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
# the next wave comes 15 s after the last raider falls
@wait 16s
# wave 2: let its raiders arrive, then strike each one until it falls
@wait 4s
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cultist,distance=..64] max 6 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_paladin,distance=..64] max 40 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_priest,distance=..64] max 60 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
# the next wave comes 15 s after the last raider falls
@wait 16s
# wave 3: let its raiders arrive, then strike each one until it falls
@wait 4s
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cultist,distance=..64] max 6 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_paladin,distance=..64] max 40 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:dragon_cult_priest,distance=..64] max 60 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2.8
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@expect chat message.the_last_sword.dragon_cult_raid_victory_reward within 30s
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:dragon_cult_raid_victory=true}]
@shot raid-won

@step S9 the dragon cult's secret letter
# the raid's priest always drops it, at the END of its death animation (the mod's mobs drop then): wait for the letter
# to be on the ground, then pick it up; with the raid won, that grants the stage
@repeat 40 until execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:dragon_cult_secret_letter"}}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
execute at @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:dragon_cult_secret_letter"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] run tp @s ~ ~ ~
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:nether_traveler_outpost=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:dragon_cult_secret_letter
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:nether_traveler_outpost=true}]

@step S10 the traveler's hold, in the Nether
@goto structure the_last_sword:travelers_hold in minecraft:the_nether
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:travelers_hold_discover=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:travelers_hold_discover=true}]
@shot travelers-hold

@step S11 the traveler's message
# the item sits in a glow item frame in the structure: a survival punch drops it (a creative one does not). The frame
# may already have popped off (its stale coordinates, PLAN.md) and left the item on the floor: either way, pick it up
execute as @e[type=minecraft:glow_item_frame,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:traveler_message"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s rotated as @s run tp @p ^ ^ ^1.5 facing entity @s
@wait 5t
@aim entity @e[type=minecraft:glow_item_frame,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:traveler_message"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] if-present
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
execute at @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:traveler_message"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] run tp @s ~ ~ ~
@wait 1s
@shot traveler-message
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:traveler_message
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:journey_to_end=true}]

@step S12 the End's reset ruins
# the mod's End structures stand in the outer End (beyond about 1000 blocks from the centre)
execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 1500 120 0
effect give @s minecraft:slow_falling 30 0 true
@goto structure the_last_sword:end_reset in minecraft:the_end
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:end_reset_discover=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:end_reset_discover=true}]
@shot end-reset

@step S13 the lost altar
@goto structure the_last_sword:end_lost_altar in minecraft:the_end
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:end_lost_altar_discover=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:end_lost_altar_discover=true}]
@shot lost-altar

@step S17 the Wound of Time
@goto structure the_last_sword:wound_of_time in minecraft:the_end
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:beyond_time=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:beyond_time=true}]
@shot wound-of-time

@step S18 the queen's trial
# she waits in the Wound of Time; coming within 4 blocks starts her boss show, at its end she is ready. One is summoned
# only if this spot has none
execute unless entity @e[type=the_last_sword:the_past_shadow_of_the_queen,distance=..96] run summon the_last_sword:the_past_shadow_of_the_queen ~ ~ ~3
execute as @e[type=the_last_sword:the_past_shadow_of_the_queen,limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s rotated as @s run tp @p ^ ^ ^2.5 facing entity @s
@expect chat bossshow.the_last_sword.the_past_shadow_of_the_queen.subtitle_2 within 30s
@wait 10s
item replace entity @s weapon.mainhand with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@aim entity the_last_sword:the_past_shadow_of_the_queen
@key key.attack
@expect chat dialogue.the_last_sword.queen.combat.death_1 within 10s
# her reward comes at death tick 100 and grants the last stage
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:proof_of_sovereignty=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:proof_of_sovereignty=true}]
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:the_givers_pain
@shot proof-of-sovereignty
# The sealed spire's stages come last: on these builds its chunk crashes the game as it generates (TLS-056, a
# known S1). Everything else in the story runs before it; once TLS-056 is fixed they run like any other stage.
@step S14 the sealed spire
@goto structure the_last_sword:sealed_spire in minecraft:the_end
# the mod checks its stages periodically (every 40 ticks): poll for this one, bounded
@repeat 20 until execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:sealed_spire_discover=true}]
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:sealed_spire_discover=true}]
@shot sealed-spire

@step S15 free the Lost Wraith
# a dragon egg on the sleeping wraith wakes it (its boss show plays, a 110-tick wake), then it must be beaten: 400
# health, each hit capped at 10. The spire's own wraith is used; one is summoned only if this spot has none
execute unless entity @e[type=the_last_sword:lost_wraith,distance=..96] run summon the_last_sword:lost_wraith ~ ~ ~4
item replace entity @s weapon.mainhand with minecraft:dragon_egg
# the spire can hold more than one wraith: every line names the nearest one, and the player steps up to it
execute as @e[type=the_last_sword:lost_wraith,limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp @p ^ ^ ^2 facing entity @s
@wait 5t
@aim entity @e[type=the_last_sword:lost_wraith,limit=1,sort=nearest]
@key key.use
@expect chat bossshow.the_last_sword.lost_wraith.subtitle_1 within 10s
@wait 8s
item replace entity @s weapon.mainhand with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
# 400 health, each hit capped at 10: a bound of 80 strikes leaves room
@repeat each @e[type=the_last_sword:lost_wraith,limit=1,sort=nearest] max 80 until execute unless entity {it}
item replace entity @s hotbar.8 with the_last_sword:the_last_sword_you_never_forgot
@key key.hotbar.9
execute as {it} run data merge entity @s {NoAI:1b}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
@end-repeat
@wait 4s
@expect chat message.the_last_sword.liberator_tower_hint within 10s
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:liberator=true}]
@shot wraith-freed

@step S16 the note: where is she?
# the item sits in a glow item frame in the structure: a survival punch drops it (a creative one does not). The frame
# may already have popped off (its stale coordinates, PLAN.md) and left the item on the floor: either way, pick it up
execute as @e[type=minecraft:glow_item_frame,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:where_is_it_note"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] at @s rotated as @s run tp @p ^ ^ ^1.5 facing entity @s
@wait 5t
@aim entity @e[type=minecraft:glow_item_frame,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:where_is_it_note"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] if-present
@key key.attack
@wait 10t
execute at @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"the_last_sword:where_is_it_note"}},limit=1,sort=nearest] run tp @s ~ ~ ~
@wait 1s
@shot where-is-it-note
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:where_is_it_note
@assert execute if entity @s[advancements={the_last_sword:queens_whereabouts=true}]

